# hilavitkutin-build

Build-time optimisation crate. cfg emission, LLVM pass configuration,
PGO/BOLT workflows, pragma system. A workspace takes it by naming
`hilavitkutin-build-pack` under `[lint-crates]` in its `mockspace.toml`,
choosing a prototype per crate in `[package.metadata.hilavitkutin-build]`
and running `mock hilavitkutin-build`, which writes the build-dependency,
each crate's `build.rs` link to the shared prototype script, the rustc
wrapper and its `.cargo/config.toml`. The pack's lint keeps all of it
as the tool writes it. The flags reach the consumer's own workspace
members only, never its dependencies.
